A||N||3||KRMFiero||Installing Foward Cradle Mounts?||||1||
Z||000000||KRMFiero||08-10-2001||12:18 AM||||Ahh this sucks, I burned out the old ones and removed the inner sleeve, cleaned the outer sleeve thingy out, but i cant get the poly cradle mounts in all the way. I called the Fiero Store and they said I had the remove this outer sleeve, that the new poly cradle mounts were designed to not use them. I tryed banging them out but i cant get them out, any tips? what should I do, what did you guys do?<P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red) Caddy 4.5 Project<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>       <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> <BR>AOL: Physcokyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-10-2001||02:28 AM||||I only remember pounding the sleeve out of the center of the backs.  The outer sleeve is part of the cradle isn't it?<P>How much off is it...do you have them going the right way?  I know I had to figure it out that they went in from the inside (uh, I guess it was right it fit better than the other way). <BR>Did you grease them up?<P>Joe<p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||08-10-2001||07:25 PM||||the new bushings are solid chunks of polly, right? They are suposed to fit tight...<P>You probly need to press them a bit. I used a big C clamp to do that. cover the small end of the bushing hole with a small chunk of tubing, I used a piece of plastic pipe, and a wood block. After the bushing is in then you stuff in the core. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||08-10-2001||07:33 PM||||They must have changed the design. I just greased mine up and pushed them into the old sleeves by hand.||||reg||1
